arxiv-2601-01770.description:
A 2026 arXiv research paper by Kenan Zhang. In this note, the author recalls the Calderon-Zygmund theory on the unit ball and derives the weak (1,1) boundedness of the projection for ℋ \mathcal{H} -harmonic Bergman space. 2020 Mathematics Subject Classification
42B20,31C05,46E22. Introduction

For
n\geqslant 2
, let
\mathbb{B}_{n}=\{x\in\mathbb{R}^{n}:|x|<1\}
be the unit ball and
\partial\mathbb{B}_{n}=\{x\in\mathbb{R}^{n}:|x|=1\}
be the unit sphere, where
|x|=(\sum_{i=1}^{n}|x_{i}|^{2})^{1/2}
is the standard Euclidean norm on
\mathbb{R}^{n}
. The hyperbolic ball is the unit ball
\mathbb{B}_{n}
equipped with the hyperbolic metric

ds^{2}=\frac{4}{(1-|x|^{2})^{2}}\sum\limits_{i=1}^{n}dx_{i}^{2}.
